<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  TEMPLATE — NOT AN INSTALLED AGENT.

  Supersedes the tracked daily-queue.worker.plist, which carried a literal
  superuser connection URL in Git. Tracked templates are credential-free, and so
  is the installed copy this one renders to: the values substituted at install
  time are a path, a Redis endpoint, and the PATH of a credential file. No
  secret is ever written into a plist.

  CREDENTIAL CONTRACT. PIPELINE_CREDENTIAL_FILE names an absolute path to a file
  containing exactly one PostgreSQL URL for the least-privilege
  ai_capital_pipeline role. bin/worker.ts reads it at startup, validates the URL
  and the exact role, and keeps the value as a local — never in the environment.
  A credential naming any other role is refused even when otherwise valid.

  ONE CREDENTIAL NAME, AND ONLY ONE. The worker receives no generic DATABASE_URL
  and no inline credential. Each stage child gets its DATABASE_URL from
  buildPipelineChildEnv(), which derives it from the validated value AFTER
  stripping every inherited database, PG* and authority variable — including
  PIPELINE_CREDENTIAL_FILE itself, so no stage can reopen the source file.

  RENDERING (the renderer now exists, and it handles no secret).
  This file is a SOURCE ARTIFACT. It is rendered by
  packages/queue/bin/render-launchd-plist.ts, which substitutes only a
  repository path, an unauthenticated Redis endpoint, and the PATH of the
  credential file. It refuses any template carrying a credential-value
  placeholder, and it parses its own output to confirm no EnvironmentVariables
  entry holds a PostgreSQL URL — mixed-case and XML-entity forms included.

  The earlier `sed` instructions were removed rather than fixed: passing a value
  through command arguments exposes it in the process table, and `sed`
  mishandles `&`, `|`, backslashes and `& < >`. The renderer escapes XML, writes
  through a private same-directory temporary, fsyncs, lints, publishes with
  link(2) so a competing writer is never destroyed, and fsyncs the directory.

    pnpm --filter @common/queue render-plist -- --agent <name> --root <abs> …

  The credential file itself is written by
  packages/queue/bin/install-pipeline-credential.ts, which reads the secret only
  from a no-echo terminal or a pre-opened descriptor — never argv or stdout.

  NOTHING HAS BEEN PROVISIONED OR INSTALLED. No credential exists, no plist is
  installed, and no agent has been started or restarted. If Time Machine
  exclusion of the credential directory is approved, it must be applied and
  verified BEFORE the credential file is first created — deleting a file does
  not remove it from existing backup history.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>com.thanapol.ai-capital.worker</string>

	<!-- caffeinate -i blocks idle sleep; npx-tsx resolves the worker entry.
	     Absolute paths so we don't depend on launchd's shell PATH. -->
	<!-- The entry point is given as an ABSOLUTE path. The superseded plist
	     passed it relative to WorkingDirectory, which works for launchd but
	     leaves a command line that names no checkout — two repositories would
	     be indistinguishable in `ps`, and the scheduler's liveness check could
	     not tell whose worker it had found. -->
	<key>ProgramArguments</key>
	<array>
		<string>/usr/bin/caffeinate</string>
		<string>-i</string>
		<string>/opt/homebrew/bin/npx</string>
		<string>tsx</string>
		<string>@@AI_CAPITAL_ROOT@@/packages/queue/bin/worker.ts</string>
	</array>

	<key>WorkingDirectory</key>
	<string>@@AI_CAPITAL_ROOT@@</string>

	<key>RunAtLoad</key>
	<true/>
	<key>KeepAlive</key>
	<true/>
	<!-- ThrottleInterval: wait 30s before respawning a freshly-crashed worker
	     so a tight crash loop doesn't burn CPU. -->
	<key>ThrottleInterval</key>
	<integer>30</integer>

	<key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
	<dict>
		<key>PATH</key>
		<string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>
		<key>PIPELINE_RUNS_DB</key>
		<string>@@AI_CAPITAL_ROOT@@/data/pipeline-runs.db</string>
		<key>DATA_ROOT</key>
		<string>@@AI_CAPITAL_ROOT@@/apps</string>
		<key>REDIS_URL</key>
		<string>@@REDIS_URL@@</string>
		<key>PIPELINE_CREDENTIAL_FILE</key>
		<string>@@PIPELINE_CREDENTIAL_FILE@@</string>
	</dict>

	<key>StandardOutPath</key>
	<string>@@AI_CAPITAL_ROOT@@/logs/queue-worker.out.log</string>
	<key>StandardErrorPath</key>
	<string>@@AI_CAPITAL_ROOT@@/logs/queue-worker.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
